---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — 방송프로그램 수출 13년. (/tv-exports)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 축인가 ──────────────────────────────────────────────
 * 2번이 「K콘텐츠 수출 — **해외 독자에게 가장 잘 팔릴 축**」으로 짚었다(후보 문서).
 * 그리고 이 표는 우리가 이미 낸 두 지면과 한 줄로 이어진다 —
 *   `/workforce` 의 스튜디오드래곤·콘텐트리가 여기 「독립제작사」다.
 *   `/watched` 의 넷플릭스 한국 작품을 만든 손이 이쪽이다.
 *
 * ── ⚠ 잔차를 숨기지 않는다 ─────────────────────────────────────
 * 네 갈래(지상파·PP·IPTV CP·독립제작사)를 더해도 **발표 총계와 안 맞는다.**
 * 2024년 기준 7.6% 가 남는다. 원표가 그 몫을 어디에도 안 붙인다.
 * 「기타」로 뭉뚱그려 채우면 없는 정밀도가 생긴다 — **남는 대로 적고 이름을 안 붙인다.**
 * 그래서 이 지면의 비중은 전부 **발표 총계** 기준이다. 네 갈래 합 기준이 아니다.
 *
 * ⛔ 방송사 이름(KBS·MBC·SBS·EBS)이 원표에 있지만 쓰지 않는다.
 *    그건 지상파 안의 세부이고, 회사끼리 줄세우는 표가 된다(순위표 금지).
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않았다. Riot Production 승인 전이다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import data from '../../data/wikitip-broadcast-export.json';

const TITLE = 'Who exports Korean television, 2012–2024';
const DESC =
  'Korean broadcast programme exports grew 5.4 times in thirteen years. Terrestrial broadcasters went '
  + 'from two-thirds of it to 4%, and independent production companies went from 7% to half. Measured, sourced.';

const rows = [...data.rows].reverse();
const 처음 = data.rows[0];
const 최신 = data.rows[data.rows.length - 1];
const cats = data.categories;

const 천달러 = (v: number | null) => (v === null ? '—' : v.toLocaleString('en-US'));
const 비중 = (v: number | null, t: number) => (v === null ? '—' : (v / t * 100).toFixed(1) + '%');
const 백만 = (v: number) => '$' + (v / 1000).toLocaleString('en-US', { maximumFractionDigits: 1 }) + 'm';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: `${data.yearFrom}/${data.yearTo}`,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://kosis.kr'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd} canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/tv-exports">
  <h1>Who exports Korean television</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Export value of Korean broadcast programmes by the kind of company that sold them, every year
    from {data.yearFrom} to {data.yearTo}. Thousands of US dollars, as published.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>The business grew. The broadcasters did not.</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Total exports went from <b>{백만(처음.total)}</b> in {data.yearFrom} to{' '}
      <b>{백만(최신.total)}</b> in {data.yearTo} — <b>{(최신.total / 처음.total).toFixed(1)}×</b>.
    </p>
    <div class="flip">
      <div>
        <span class="lab">Terrestrial broadcasters</span>
        <span class="big">{비중(처음.parts['Terrestrial broadcasters'], 처음.total)} → {비중(최신.parts['Terrestrial broadcasters'], 최신.total)}</span>
        <span class="det">
          {백만(처음.parts['Terrestrial broadcasters']!)} → {백만(최신.parts['Terrestrial broadcasters']!)} ·
          peaked at {백만(data.rows.find((r) => r.year === 2014)!.parts['Terrestrial broadcasters']!)} in 2014
        </span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="lab">Independent production companies</span>
        <span class="big">{비중(처음.parts['Independent production companies'], 처음.total)} → {비중(최신.parts['Independent production companies'], 최신.total)}</span>
        <span class="det">
          {백만(처음.parts['Independent production companies']!)} → {백만(최신.parts['Independent production companies']!)} ·
          now the largest single category
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      The companies in that second row are the ones that make the drama series the world streams —
      several of them are listed, and we count their staff on
      {' '}<a href="/workforce">the workforce page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Every year, by kind of company</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Thousands of US dollars. Share is of that year's <b>published total</b>, not of the four
      categories added together — they do not add up, and the gap is shown.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Year</th><th>Total</th>{cats.map((c) => <th>{c}</th>)}<th>Unattributed</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {rows.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="yr">{r.year}</td>
              <td class="tot">{천달러(r.total)}</td>
              {cats.map((c) => (
                <td>
                  {천달러((r.parts as Record<string, number | null>)[c])}
                  <span class="pc">{비중((r.parts as Record<string, number | null>)[c], r.total)}</span>
                </td>
              ))}
              <td class="res">{천달러(r.residual)}<span class="pc">{비중(r.residual, r.total)}</span></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/tv-exports" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where these numbers come from</h2>
    <ul>
      {/* ⛔ 영어 앞 · 원어 괄호 안. 손님이 영어권이다(2026-08-10 손님 걷기) */}
      <li><b>{data.source}</b> ({data.sourceKo}). Unit: {data.unit}.</li>
      <li>
        <b>The categories add to the total.</b> In {data.yearTo} the four kinds of company account for
        {' '}{천달러(최신.named)} of a published {천달러(최신.total)}, exactly. Across all
        {' '}{data.rows.length} years the largest gap is ${data.reconciled.maxResidual},000, which is rounding.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>🔴 Corrected 2026-08-07.</b> This page previously showed a {비중(95258, 최신.total)} residual it
        could not attribute. There was no residual. The source classifies exports on two levels — the form
        of export above, the type of company below — and returns only the lower name, so several rows a
        year read “terrestrial broadcasters” and differ by code alone. We had taken the finished-programme
        row for three of the four types while the fourth entered whole. Each type is now the sum of every
        export form published for it, checked against the survey’s own subtotal in the
        {' '}{data.reconciled.checkedAgainstPublishedSubtotal} cells where it publishes one — agreeing to
        within ${data.reconciled.maxSubtotalGap},000.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Missing years.</b> IPTV content providers appear only from 2023, which is when the survey
        began reporting them separately. Blank means the survey published no value, not zero.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>What this does not say.</b> The source also breaks terrestrial exports down by individual
        broadcaster. We do not reproduce that — it turns a structural picture into a league table of
        companies, and this page is about the shape of the industry, not a ranking of firms.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      Sources: KOSIS (국가데이터처) and the Content Industry Survey (한국콘텐츠진흥원 「콘텐츠산업조사」),
      figures to {data.yearTo}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="back"><a href="/">&larr; Back to the front page</a></p>
</WikiTip>

<style>
  h1 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.7rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--muted); }
  section { margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .4rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .sub { font-size: .87rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .note { font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); margin: .9rem 0 0; line-height: 1.6; }

  /* 뒤집힘을 두 칸으로 나란히 — 표를 읽기 전에 결론이 먼저 보이게 */
  .flip { display: grid; gap: .8rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr; margin: 1rem 0 0; }
  @media (min-width: 34rem) { .flip { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .flip > div { background: var(--card); border-radius: 8px; padding: .9rem 1rem; }
  .lab { display: block; font-size: .76rem; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase;
         color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700; }
  .big { display: block; font-size: 1.32rem; font-weight: 700; margin: .25rem 0 .3rem;
         letter-spacing: -.01em; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .det { display: block; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; }

  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .84rem; }
  th, td { padding: .45rem .55rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: right;
           white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  th { font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .03em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
       font-weight: 700; }
  th:first-child, td.yr { text-align: left; }
  td.yr, td.tot { font-weight: 700; }
  td.res { color: var(--muted); }
  .pc { display: block; font-size: .72rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400; }
  tbody tr:first-child { background: var(--card); }

  .src ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; }
  .src li { margin: .45rem 0; }
  .src b { color: var(--ink); }
  .back { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: .9rem; }
</style>
